### Nesting (#1184, TYP-50)

Several `Supervise(b).OnFailure(match, strategy)` layers may be nested. A failed turn is taken by the **innermost layer whose matcher selects the cause**; an exhausted `WithLimit` is rethrown to the next outer layer that matches. Scope: [`docs/scopes/1184-innermost-supervision.md`](../docs/scopes/1184-innermost-supervision.md). Oracles: [typed-nested-supervision-2026-11-06](../docs/parity/oracles/typed-nested-supervision-2026-11-06.md) (scenarios N1 to N11) and [typed-resume-2026-11-06](../docs/parity/oracles/typed-resume-2026-11-06.md) (R5a to R5e), both executed on Pekko 1.7.1, 3 runs each. Record: [`EXECUTION-RECORD.md`](../migration/stage-1/typed-1184-innermost/EXECUTION-RECORD.md). Tests: [`nested_innermost_test.go`](typed/nested_innermost_test.go), [`nested_replacement_test.go`](typed/nested_replacement_test.go).

- **Implemented: the innermost matching layer decides.** A cause is handled by the innermost layer whose matcher selects it, also when the matchers overlap or are equal and the outer layer has another strategy (`TestNested_InnermostMatchWins`: three rows); oracle R5c, R5d, R5e. The specs `SupervisionSpec.scala:201-211` and `:849` use disjoint classes and back R5a and R5b only.
- **Implemented: an exhausted inner limit reaches the next outer layer** of a different matcher, which handles it by its own strategy, `Resume` or `Restart` (`TestNested_ExhaustedLimitReachesOuter`); oracle N2, N7d.
- **Implemented: a supervised behavior returned by a handler.** With an equal matcher it replaces the enclosing layer; with a different matcher it is added and both stay (`TestNested_ReturnedSuperviseReplacesEqual`, `TestNested_ReturnedSuperviseKeepsDifferent`); oracle N3, N11 and N4. The first row of the first test (N3, a returned `Resume`) passes even if the enclosing layer is kept, because the innermost layer decides anyway; its second row (a returned limited `Restart`, the shape of N11) is the one that fails then.
- **Implemented: equal-matcher layers are deduplicated once a stack has started** (the inner layer replaces the enclosing one), at three sites: the initial start (`TestNested_EqualMatcherReplacesAfterStart`, `TestNested_EqualMatcherInnerRethrowStops`; oracle N1, N7, N6c), the stack a handler returns (`TestNested_ReturnedStackDedupes`; N9) and the stack a restart rebuilds (`TestNested_RebuiltStackDedupes`; N10). **Not while the start is failing:** every layer is consulted in turn (`TestRestartLimit_InitialStart`; N8). Rule: [ADR 0035](../docs/adr/0035-typed-supervision.md), Amendment (2026-11-06); Pekko `InterceptorImpl.scala:82-85` (`aroundStart`, then `deduplicate`) and `:106-122`, `Supervision.scala:78-83` (two supervisors are the same when their throwable classes are equal, the strategy is not compared).
- **Inferred, not observed.** That the layers are deduplicated is concluded from the effects (the actor stops where an outer layer would have taken the rethrow); no log line of the oracle shows the stack of supervisors. The same holds for the rethrow itself (`Supervision.scala:335-337`).
- **No flattened form (Owner decision D-3).** Pekko's `supervise(b).onFailure(..).onFailure(..)` has no Go counterpart: `OnFailure` returns a `Behavior`, so only the nested form exists. The oracle shows both forms give the same events (N5a).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  S[stack of layers collected] -->|start fails| C[every layer is consulted in turn, no deduplication]
  S -->|start succeeds| D[dedupeLayers: an inner layer replaces an enclosing one of the same matcher]
  H[a handler returns a stack] --> D
  R[a restart rebuilds the stack] --> D
  D --> M[a failure goes to the innermost matching layer; an exhausted limit goes outward]
```

