## Stash (#889, TYP-13)

Scope: [`docs/scopes/889-typed-stash-buffer.md`](../docs/scopes/889-typed-stash-buffer.md). Record: [`EXECUTION-RECORD.md`](../migration/stage-1/typed-889-stash-buffer/EXECUTION-RECORD.md).
Source: [`typed/stash.go`](typed/stash.go). Runnable: [`ExampleWithStash`](typed/example_test.go).

`WithStash(capacity, factory)` is `Behaviors.withStash` (`Behaviors.scala:45-49`) built over `Setup`: it creates an empty `*StashBuffer[T]` of the given
capacity and returns the behavior `factory` returns. A behavior holds a message of its own protocol in the buffer while it is not ready for it, and asks the buffer
about its state. `Unstash` and `UnstashAll` replay what it holds (#927, see "Replay" below).

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  S[Spawn or restart] --> W[WithStash runs Setup]
  W --> B[new empty StashBuffer bound to the Context]
  B --> F[factory returns the behavior]
  F -->|Stash on a full buffer| O[ErrStashOverflow returned, buffer intact]
  O -->|handler returns it| X[Supervise decides: Resume, Restart or default Stop]
```

- **Implemented:** `Stash`, `Head`, `Size`, `Capacity`, `IsEmpty`, `NonEmpty`, `IsFull`, `ForEach` (insertion order, nothing removed), `Exists`, `Clear` and the package function `Contains`
  (`==` of a comparable `T`; a Go method cannot add the constraint). Tests: [`stash_test.go`](typed/stash_test.go) (S1 to S7c), [`stash_withstash_test.go`](typed/stash_withstash_test.go) (S8, S9).
- **Errors instead of exceptions.** `Stash` on a full buffer returns an error that wraps `ErrStashOverflow` and leaves the buffer as it was (Pekko throws `StashOverflowException`); `Head` of an empty buffer returns
  `ErrStashEmpty` (Pekko throws `NoSuchElementException`). Match with `errors.Is`; the text is not API. A handler that returns the overflow error is a failed turn: `Supervise(b).OnFailure(ErrorIs(ErrStashOverflow), Resume())`
  keeps the actor and the buffer, `Restart()` reruns `Setup` and so builds a **new empty buffer**, and an unmatched cause takes the default Stop (test `TestWithStash_OverflowIsCaughtBySupervision`).
- **Confinement.** The buffer is actor-confined and not safe for concurrent use; it has no locks, as Pekko's. Use it only inside the behavior that received it. Calling `Stash` or `Clear` from the callback of `ForEach` is **unsupported**.
- **Capacity is not validated,** as in Pekko: 0 is full from the start (the first `Stash` overflows) and a negative capacity is never full, so the buffer is unbounded.
- **The zero value is a message.** Pekko rejects `null` (`StashBufferImpl.scala:72`); Go has no null, so `""`, `0` or a nil pointer is stashed and counted. No `ErrNilMessage` exists.
- **No constructor.** `StashBuffer[T]` is a struct pointer with unexported fields, and `WithStash` is the only way to get one (Pekko's `StashBuffer.apply` is `private[pekko]`).
- **Separate capacity:** the restart stash has its own bound (`WithStashCapacity`, see "Supervision and restart"); the user-facing `StashBuffer` above is bounded by its own capacity. `Stopped` (#1182) and its interruption of replay (#927 slice C) are implemented; see "Stopped" and "Replay".
- **Evidence (ADR 0033 D13):** the buffer rows are read against `StashBufferImpl.scala`, `StashBuffer.scala` and `StashBufferSpec.scala` (v1.7.1), not run. Capacity 0 and negative, the zero value and the overflow under `OnFailure` have no Pekko
  test (alternative evidence; S9 approved by the Owner on 2026-11-10). No Typed parity is claimed.

### Replay (#927 slices A1, A2, B and C, TYP-14, with #1169)

Scope: [`docs/scopes/927-typed-unstash.md`](../docs/scopes/927-typed-unstash.md). Source: [`typed/unstash.go`](typed/unstash.go). Tests: [`unstash_test.go`](typed/unstash_test.go) (U1, U3, U4, U5, U8, D-6) and [`unstash_same_test.go`](typed/unstash_same_test.go) (U2, U6, U7, the Supervise layers) and [`unstash_fail_test.go`](typed/unstash_fail_test.go) (F1, F2, D-4) and [`unstash_stopped_test.go`](typed/unstash_stopped_test.go) (S1-S5).

`UnstashAll(behavior)` and `Unstash(behavior, n, wrap)` give the first messages of the buffer, one at a time and in order, to `behavior` and to the behavior each one returns
(`StashBufferImpl.scala:156-185, 192-216`), and return `(Behavior[T], error)`: the final behavior, which the handler returns.

- **Eager.** The replay runs inside the call, as Pekko's. Only the messages present at the call are replayed (one stashed by a handler waits for the next call), a `Clear` in a handler ends it, an `n` of zero or less replays nothing but starts the behavior, and an empty buffer returns the behavior unstarted.
